WEBVTT

1
00:00:16,917 --> 00:00:18,000
[whoops]

2
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:27,750
[whooshes]

3
00:00:30,042 --> 00:00:31,875
- [humming]
- [grunts]

4
00:00:37,125 --> 00:00:38,292
[both grunting]

5
00:00:38,375 --> 00:00:40,167
[laughs hysterically]

6
00:00:54,208 --> 00:00:56,208
[intriguing music playing]

7
00:01:00,042 --> 00:01:02,167
Well, kid, ready for our assignment?

8
00:01:02,250 --> 00:01:03,292
[laughing gleefully]

9
00:01:03,375 --> 00:01:05,333
Look, if you're gonna be a bounty hunter,

10
00:01:05,417 --> 00:01:07,667
you'll have to sound more intimidating
than that.

11
00:01:07,750 --> 00:01:08,750
[clears throat]

12
00:01:08,833 --> 00:01:10,375
[laughs wickedly]

13
00:01:11,125 --> 00:01:13,833
[sighs] Coruscant wasn't built in a day.

14
00:01:14,375 --> 00:01:15,625
Let's go meet our contact.

15
00:01:15,708 --> 00:01:16,958
[hums]

16
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:19,958
[whoops]

17
00:01:20,042 --> 00:01:21,417
[Mando] Be careful in here.

18
00:01:21,542 --> 00:01:22,958
We have powerful enemies.

19
00:01:23,042 --> 00:01:25,500
Like those pirates we ran out of Nevarro.

20
00:01:25,583 --> 00:01:27,667
So stay alert.
We don't want any--

21
00:01:27,750 --> 00:01:29,500
- [all] Surprise!
- [Mando] Ahh!

22
00:01:29,583 --> 00:01:31,417
[all screaming]

23
00:01:38,375 --> 00:01:39,417
Suprise?

24
00:01:40,833 --> 00:01:41,833
Peli!

25
00:01:41,917 --> 00:01:43,208
What are you doing here?

26
00:01:43,292 --> 00:01:46,417
I'm supposed to meet a contact
for an important assignment.

27
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:48,417
Your contact was Peli.

28
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:53,542
<i>Hey Mando, I got a big time
bounty-huntin' job for you, see?</i>

29
00:01:53,625 --> 00:01:56,833
<i>And bring that cute kid with you too, see?</i>

30
00:01:56,917 --> 00:01:58,500
<i>Uh, hey, get out of the shot!</i>

31
00:01:58,833 --> 00:01:59,833
[clears throat]

32
00:01:59,917 --> 00:02:03,083
<i>And I ain't Peli Motto in disguise, see?</i>

33
00:02:03,875 --> 00:02:05,208
Wait. You?

34
00:02:05,292 --> 00:02:06,625
Were Tough-o Guy-o?

35
00:02:06,708 --> 00:02:09,042
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
But it's all good because you came!

36
00:02:09,125 --> 00:02:11,333
Now we can have this party
with all your friends.

37
00:02:11,417 --> 00:02:14,792
And we can show you how much we appreciate
everything you've done for us.

38
00:02:15,958 --> 00:02:17,042
We're leaving.

39
00:02:17,625 --> 00:02:21,958
Mando, you are gonna have fun today
whether you have fun or not.

40
00:02:22,042 --> 00:02:25,792
You Mandalorians all say,
"This is the way".

41
00:02:25,875 --> 00:02:29,125
Well, for today,
this is the way, right, buddy?

42
00:02:29,208 --> 00:02:32,333
[intriguing music playing]

43
00:02:37,958 --> 00:02:39,833
[Mando sighs deeply]

44
00:02:39,917 --> 00:02:42,167
- [all cheering]
- Let's party!

45
00:02:42,250 --> 00:02:45,167
[upbeat music playing]

46
00:02:47,625 --> 00:02:50,333
Mando, where did you get
all these friends?

47
00:02:50,417 --> 00:02:52,208
I thought you kept to yourself?

48
00:02:52,292 --> 00:02:53,708
Oh, he did.

49
00:02:53,792 --> 00:02:58,792
Din Djarin here was the loneliest loner
who ever loned.

50
00:02:58,875 --> 00:03:01,042
- Till that kid came along.
- [all exclaiming]

51
00:03:01,125 --> 00:03:03,083
It's one heck of a tale!

52
00:03:03,167 --> 00:03:05,167
I don't like to talk about myself.

53
00:03:05,250 --> 00:03:07,125
Well, good thing I do!

54
00:03:07,208 --> 00:03:08,375
Gather around, everyone.

55
00:03:08,458 --> 00:03:10,000
I'll tell you the exciting story

56
00:03:10,083 --> 00:03:13,625
of how a little green kid
turned a stone-cold bounty hunter

57
00:03:13,708 --> 00:03:16,625
into a warm and fuzzy
stone-cold bounty hunter.

58
00:03:16,708 --> 00:03:19,667
How could you tell our story?

59
00:03:19,750 --> 00:03:22,000
You were only there for a tiny part of it.

60
00:03:22,083 --> 00:03:23,833
I'm a mechanic at a spaceport.

61
00:03:23,917 --> 00:03:25,875
Everybody tells me everything.

62
00:03:25,958 --> 00:03:30,375
So, the way I hear it,
is it all went down like this.

63
00:03:30,458 --> 00:03:32,833
<i>Mando had just come back
from some bounty-hunting</i>

64
00:03:32,917 --> 00:03:35,625
<i>with a ship
full of captured bad guys on ice.</i>

65
00:03:36,167 --> 00:03:39,833
<i>This day, Mando got the assignment
that would change his life.</i>

66
00:03:40,292 --> 00:03:43,250
The Mandalorian, meet your new client.

67
00:03:43,333 --> 00:03:45,708
He is called The Client.

68
00:03:45,792 --> 00:03:48,250
- [sniffs]
- That's it? The Client?

69
00:03:48,333 --> 00:03:52,000
Yes, we share the same first name, "The".

70
00:03:52,458 --> 00:03:54,833
Dr. Pershing, and I desire for you

71
00:03:54,917 --> 00:03:58,542
to go to Arvala-7
and acquire an asset for us.

72
00:03:58,625 --> 00:04:00,500
This asset is called--

73
00:04:00,583 --> 00:04:01,958
The Asset?

74
00:04:02,042 --> 00:04:05,208
Your powers of perspicacity
are remarkable.

75
00:04:05,292 --> 00:04:08,958
Now, I cannot divulge
the asset's identity to you,

76
00:04:09,042 --> 00:04:13,167
nor tell you its height,
color or shape of its ears.

77
00:04:13,250 --> 00:04:16,167
I can only say it is 50 years old,

78
00:04:16,250 --> 00:04:20,958
which, by any measure, you and I go by,
is quite old.

79
00:04:21,042 --> 00:04:22,792
Why did you say that so weird?

80
00:04:22,875 --> 00:04:25,958
I did it... for reasons.

81
00:04:26,042 --> 00:04:27,750
Here is your first payment.

82
00:04:27,833 --> 00:04:32,583
Something Mandalorians greatly treasure,
Beskar steel.

83
00:04:32,667 --> 00:04:34,792
When you deliver the asset to me,

84
00:04:34,875 --> 00:04:38,792
there will be much more
from where that came from.

85
00:04:38,875 --> 00:04:39,875
- [crashes]
- [screams]

86
00:04:40,458 --> 00:04:41,958
[Peli] <i>So Mando took the Beskar</i>

87
00:04:42,042 --> 00:04:47,542
<i>to the last refuge of the Mandalorians
on Nevarro, the forge of The Armorer.</i>

88
00:04:47,625 --> 00:04:49,292
- [hissing]
- [clangs]

89
00:04:53,375 --> 00:04:54,875
[Armorer] For you.

90
00:04:54,958 --> 00:04:57,042
This is the Way.

91
00:04:57,125 --> 00:04:58,167
This is the Way.

92
00:04:58,250 --> 00:05:01,542
Now I must go
and fulfill my bounty-hunting contract.

93
00:05:01,625 --> 00:05:02,750
This is the Way.

94
00:05:03,542 --> 00:05:05,792
Can you show me where the door is?

95
00:05:05,875 --> 00:05:07,458
This is the Way.

96
00:05:07,542 --> 00:05:12,333
Wait. Are you saying this is the way out,
or just "This is the Way"?

97
00:05:13,833 --> 00:05:15,667
- This is the Way.
- Ugh.

98
00:05:15,750 --> 00:05:17,667
I'll find the exit on my own.

99
00:05:17,750 --> 00:05:20,458
[Peli] <i>To capture his bounty,
Mando went to Arvala-7.</i>

100
00:05:20,542 --> 00:05:25,167
It's a desolate planet, but way classier
than the other six Arvalas, oof!

101
00:05:25,250 --> 00:05:28,917
<i>There, he was aided
by a wise Ugnaught named Kuiil</i>

102
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,417
{\an8}<i>who led him
to where The Asset was being held.</i>

103
00:05:32,833 --> 00:05:34,417
{\an8}Ugh, pirates.

104
00:05:36,250 --> 00:05:38,458
{\an8}I command you to produce the asset.

105
00:05:38,542 --> 00:05:40,833
And a competing bounty droid.

106
00:05:40,917 --> 00:05:42,083
- [gun cocking]
- [gunfire]

107
00:05:45,208 --> 00:05:46,792
Who's a showoff.

108
00:05:51,750 --> 00:05:53,833
That-- That droid was doing the robot.

109
00:05:55,500 --> 00:05:56,750
[grunting]

110
00:05:58,292 --> 00:05:59,458
[grunts]

111
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:02,708
[Peli] <i>Mando fought his way
to the fortress</i>

112
00:06:02,792 --> 00:06:07,792
<i>and convinced that deadly droid
to work with him and split the reward.</i>

113
00:06:08,958 --> 00:06:11,625
We're surrounded,
but I think we can beat these guys.

114
00:06:11,708 --> 00:06:15,792
[Droid] Negative. My manufacturer
protocols dictate I cannot be captured.

115
00:06:15,875 --> 00:06:18,542
Initiating self-destruct sequencing.

116
00:06:18,625 --> 00:06:19,750
Don't self-destruct!

117
00:06:19,833 --> 00:06:21,500
- Are you nuts?
- [soldier grunts]

118
00:06:21,583 --> 00:06:22,958
My sanity has been questioned.

119
00:06:23,042 --> 00:06:26,042
- Initiating self-destruct sequencing.
- [alarm blaring]

120
00:06:26,458 --> 00:06:28,167
Stop it, you crazy hunk of junk.

121
00:06:28,250 --> 00:06:29,875
You have called me a nasty name.

122
00:06:29,958 --> 00:06:31,875
- Initiating self--
- [grunts]

123
00:06:32,458 --> 00:06:34,583
[Peli] <i>Things went on like that for a bit.</i>

124
00:06:35,708 --> 00:06:37,917
[Droid] It might rain later,
initiating, so--

125
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:39,833
That's enough!

126
00:06:39,917 --> 00:06:40,917
Uh-oh!

127
00:06:41,750 --> 00:06:43,000
[explosion]

128
00:06:44,833 --> 00:06:47,292
Let's get this 50-year-old asset.

129
00:06:47,375 --> 00:06:50,333
[device beeping]

130
00:06:54,042 --> 00:06:56,042
It's just a kid.

131
00:06:56,125 --> 00:06:58,167
[Droid] I am programmed to terminate.

132
00:07:00,667 --> 00:07:01,667
[gunshot]

133
00:07:01,750 --> 00:07:02,833
No.

134
00:07:02,917 --> 00:07:04,083
[thudding]

135
00:07:09,250 --> 00:07:13,042
[Peli] <i>Mando's tough shell
cracked a teensy bit that day,</i>

136
00:07:13,125 --> 00:07:17,958
but there was one little problem
in bringing the kid back to the client.

137
00:07:18,042 --> 00:07:20,500
<i>Well, actually,
a whole bunch of little problems.</i>

138
00:07:20,583 --> 00:07:23,583
[all whooping]

139
00:07:25,125 --> 00:07:27,708
My ship! I just had it waxed.

140
00:07:27,792 --> 00:07:32,917
[Peli] <i>Kuiil talked to the Jawas, and he
got them to promise to fix Mando's ship</i>

141
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:38,583
<i>if he fought a beast called a mudhorn
and got one of its precious eggs.</i>

142
00:07:38,667 --> 00:07:39,667
[Mando grunts]

143
00:07:41,417 --> 00:07:43,167
[grunting]

144
00:07:47,125 --> 00:07:48,875
[Jawas whooping]

145
00:07:49,792 --> 00:07:50,792
[coos]

146
00:07:50,875 --> 00:07:53,750
Yeah, I like you, too,
but this is no time to be adorable.

147
00:07:53,833 --> 00:07:54,833
[roars]

148
00:07:58,292 --> 00:07:59,625
[swishing]

149
00:08:03,167 --> 00:08:04,750
[mudhorn grunts]

150
00:08:07,958 --> 00:08:13,000
[Mando] It's like he's moving that thing
with some kind of unseen force.

151
00:08:13,083 --> 00:08:15,542
It is called the Force.

152
00:08:15,625 --> 00:08:18,417
They have got to work
on better names for stuff.

153
00:08:18,500 --> 00:08:20,583
[exhilarating instrumental music playing]

154
00:08:21,750 --> 00:08:22,792
[mudhorn grunts]

155
00:08:22,875 --> 00:08:24,000
[whooping triumphantly]

156
00:08:31,833 --> 00:08:33,042
[laughs]

157
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:35,875
[Peli] <i>With the kid's help,
Mando got the egg...</i>

158
00:08:35,958 --> 00:08:37,542
[speaking in foreign language]

159
00:08:37,625 --> 00:08:39,208
<i>...and his ship back.</i>

160
00:08:39,292 --> 00:08:41,625
[speaking in foreign language]

161
00:08:45,958 --> 00:08:47,625
[Mando] Ooh-Teeny.

162
00:08:51,375 --> 00:08:56,500
[Peli] <i>So Mando took the kid back
to the client to fulfill his assignment.</i>

163
00:08:56,583 --> 00:08:57,958
[both] Aww!

164
00:08:58,042 --> 00:09:00,833
Cease that! We are Imperial Remnants.

165
00:09:00,917 --> 00:09:02,583
We do not "aww"!

166
00:09:02,667 --> 00:09:03,708
[both] Aww!

167
00:09:03,792 --> 00:09:06,625
Stop it. Here is
your payment, Mandalorian.

168
00:09:06,708 --> 00:09:10,833
Now you may take one last
wistful look at the adorable child

169
00:09:10,917 --> 00:09:14,458
before we do terrible,
horrible, painful things to it.

170
00:09:16,625 --> 00:09:17,708
[whimpers]

171
00:09:17,792 --> 00:09:20,083
[somber instrumental music playing]

172
00:09:21,250 --> 00:09:22,333
No!

173
00:09:22,417 --> 00:09:26,292
[Peli] <i>All of a sudden,
Mando had the X Empire after him.</i>

174
00:09:26,375 --> 00:09:29,083
<i>The hunter was now the hunted,</i>

175
00:09:29,167 --> 00:09:32,333
<i>and then the most exciting thing happened.</i>

176
00:09:32,417 --> 00:09:34,250
- They met me!
- [laughs]

177
00:09:34,333 --> 00:09:35,833
[grunts]

178
00:09:35,917 --> 00:09:37,125
[Peli] <i>The end!</i>

179
00:09:37,208 --> 00:09:38,750
- [Jawas cheering]
- [giggles]

180
00:09:41,333 --> 00:09:42,833
[Mando] Wait, wait, stop.

181
00:09:42,917 --> 00:09:45,792
[grunts] A whole bunch
of other stuff happened.

182
00:09:45,875 --> 00:09:48,333
Ugh. Fine.
You know I'm not getting paid for this.

183
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:52,833
[Peli] <i>So Mando tangled
with the lethal Fennec Shand,</i>

184
00:09:52,917 --> 00:09:55,250
<i>and then teamed up
with some nasty bad guys</i>

185
00:09:55,333 --> 00:09:59,417
<i>to free another nasty bad guy
from a grody prison transport.</i>

186
00:09:59,500 --> 00:10:03,750
<i>But the nasty bad guys were so nasty
that they double crossed Mando.</i>

187
00:10:03,833 --> 00:10:06,833
<i>And so he ended up putting them all
in the prison ship,</i>

188
00:10:06,917 --> 00:10:08,583
which is where I got this mug.

189
00:10:08,667 --> 00:10:09,750
[Jawas gasping]

190
00:10:10,250 --> 00:10:12,125
Come on, Mando.
It's not how it looks.

191
00:10:12,208 --> 00:10:13,958
We betrayed you for money!

192
00:10:15,083 --> 00:10:17,833
[Peli] <i>All the fighting and fleeing
was just exhausting.</i>

193
00:10:17,917 --> 00:10:20,042
<i>- Oh, can you imagine?</i>
- [honks]

194
00:10:20,583 --> 00:10:24,000
<i>So Mando was happy
when his old friend, Greef Karga,</i>

195
00:10:24,083 --> 00:10:28,667
<i>called with an offer to return to Navarro
for a truce with the bounty hunters.</i>

196
00:10:28,750 --> 00:10:31,333
<i>Mando, buddy, come on back.</i>

197
00:10:31,417 --> 00:10:33,292
<i>I swear this is not a trick.</i>

198
00:10:33,375 --> 00:10:34,375
<i>It was a trick!</i>

199
00:10:34,458 --> 00:10:37,083
He was just luring Mando
back to ambush him.

200
00:10:37,167 --> 00:10:38,542
[all booing]

201
00:10:38,625 --> 00:10:39,917
I said I'm sorry!

202
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,792
I made it up to Mando
and helped them escape.

203
00:10:42,875 --> 00:10:46,667
<i>Greef organized a plan to take out
the bad guys once and for all.</i>

204
00:10:46,750 --> 00:10:50,875
<i>And Kuiil helped by making sure the kid
would be protected during the battle.</i>

205
00:10:51,625 --> 00:10:54,667
You, my sensors, detect awkwardness.

206
00:10:54,750 --> 00:10:56,500
Do not fear, IG-11.

207
00:10:56,583 --> 00:10:57,958
I have spoken.

208
00:10:58,042 --> 00:11:00,250
This thing is a deadly threat.

209
00:11:00,333 --> 00:11:01,375
Not anymore.

210
00:11:01,458 --> 00:11:03,167
I have spoken again.

211
00:11:03,250 --> 00:11:06,292
Now my primary function
is to protect the child.

212
00:11:06,375 --> 00:11:09,333
He has been reprogrammed by me.

213
00:11:09,417 --> 00:11:11,667
I have spoken again.

214
00:11:11,750 --> 00:11:13,458
- Again.
- No way.

215
00:11:13,542 --> 00:11:16,000
Once a killer, always a killer.

216
00:11:16,083 --> 00:11:18,042
You do not trust my nurturing instincts.

217
00:11:18,125 --> 00:11:19,458
Initiating self-destruct.

218
00:11:19,542 --> 00:11:20,833
- Okay, okay, fine.
- [alarm blaring]

219
00:11:20,917 --> 00:11:22,083
You can watch the kid.

220
00:11:22,167 --> 00:11:24,083
Now let's go take out those Imperials.

221
00:11:26,667 --> 00:11:27,750
[both gasping]

222
00:11:29,125 --> 00:11:30,125
[grunts]

223
00:11:30,625 --> 00:11:31,708
[grunts]

224
00:11:33,583 --> 00:11:36,292
[all screaming]

225
00:11:36,458 --> 00:11:37,667
[gasps]

226
00:11:37,750 --> 00:11:42,250
I am also experiencing
terror of the pew pew pews!

227
00:11:42,333 --> 00:11:44,417
They're gone. We win!

228
00:11:48,208 --> 00:11:50,542
They're back. We lose!

229
00:11:50,625 --> 00:11:53,208
[dramatic music playing]

230
00:11:55,708 --> 00:12:00,833
[Peli] <i>It was Moff Gideon, a super scary
former Imperial big cheese.</i>

231
00:12:00,917 --> 00:12:03,208
He was the one who wanted
the kid the whole time.

232
00:12:03,292 --> 00:12:04,292
[all booing]

233
00:12:07,250 --> 00:12:09,625
Hand over that 50-year-old child.

234
00:12:09,708 --> 00:12:12,708
There's nowhere to run, Mandalorian.

235
00:12:14,042 --> 00:12:15,917
This is the Way. Down!

236
00:12:16,750 --> 00:12:18,708
- [all exclaiming]
- After them!

237
00:12:18,792 --> 00:12:22,708
I need that child... for reasons!

238
00:12:22,792 --> 00:12:25,167
[all scream]

239
00:12:26,333 --> 00:12:30,167
[Peli] <i>And they made a run for it
in the lava river under Nevarro.</i>

240
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:32,125
Just a bit further, and we'll be safe.

241
00:12:32,208 --> 00:12:35,167
Next up, Imperial Ambush station.

242
00:12:35,625 --> 00:12:36,750
Ambush station?

243
00:12:38,292 --> 00:12:41,250
Stormtroopers.
This is gonna be a tough fight.

244
00:12:41,333 --> 00:12:43,917
[Droid] Negative.
I am programmed to protect the child.

245
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:48,667
To fulfill my function, I will engage
the enemy alone and self-destruct.

246
00:12:48,750 --> 00:12:50,917
Thank you for your sacrifice.

247
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,500
Uh, aren't you going to stop me?

248
00:12:52,583 --> 00:12:54,583
No, you're right.

249
00:12:54,667 --> 00:12:57,792
- This is the only way to save the child.
- [squeals]

250
00:12:57,875 --> 00:13:00,083
Me and my big
speech processing unit.

251
00:13:00,625 --> 00:13:05,208
Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

252
00:13:05,292 --> 00:13:07,292
I am melting so slowly. Ow!

253
00:13:07,375 --> 00:13:09,042
Ow! Ow!

254
00:13:09,125 --> 00:13:11,833
Greetings, troopers,
please stand there doing nothing

255
00:13:11,917 --> 00:13:12,958
while I activate this

256
00:13:13,042 --> 00:13:14,833
- beeping thing in my chest.
- [alarm beeping]

257
00:13:14,917 --> 00:13:16,333
[stormtroopers yelling]

258
00:13:18,875 --> 00:13:22,042
[Peli] <i>It looked like they were saved,
but, uh-uh!</i>

259
00:13:23,958 --> 00:13:25,125
[laughs wickedly]

260
00:13:25,625 --> 00:13:26,708
Moff Gideon!

261
00:13:28,792 --> 00:13:30,875
[gunfire]

262
00:13:39,083 --> 00:13:42,042
[laughs wickedly]

263
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,417
You can't touch me in here, Mando!

264
00:13:46,500 --> 00:13:49,708
[laughs wickedly]

265
00:13:49,792 --> 00:13:52,083
- Uh-oh!
- [beeping]

266
00:13:52,167 --> 00:13:55,292
I told the Empire to put
windshield wipers on these things.

267
00:13:55,375 --> 00:13:56,583
[explosion]

268
00:14:00,542 --> 00:14:02,625
Uh, do you think we should go make sure

269
00:14:02,708 --> 00:14:06,250
Moff Gideon didn't somehow
survive that crash?

270
00:14:07,125 --> 00:14:08,208
[both] Nah.

271
00:14:14,542 --> 00:14:17,042
I will get that child yet.

272
00:14:17,125 --> 00:14:18,708
- [phone beeping]
- [line ringing]

273
00:14:18,792 --> 00:14:21,208
Mom, can you come pick me up?

274
00:14:22,958 --> 00:14:27,708
That was a noble sacrifice
IG-11 made to save the child,

275
00:14:27,792 --> 00:14:32,000
- blowing himself to pieces like that.
- I did what I had to do.

276
00:14:32,083 --> 00:14:33,083
[exclaims]

277
00:14:33,167 --> 00:14:35,208
How are you here?
You self-destructed!

278
00:14:35,292 --> 00:14:37,542
I got better, then I got destroyed again.

279
00:14:37,625 --> 00:14:39,917
Then I got better again.
It's sort of what I do.

280
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:41,000
- [distant explosion]
- [all exclaim]

281
00:14:41,083 --> 00:14:42,083
What was that?

282
00:14:44,417 --> 00:14:45,750
- Imperials!
- [gun cocking]

283
00:14:54,833 --> 00:14:55,833
[guns cocking]

284
00:14:56,375 --> 00:14:59,333
Wow, it stinks to be those guys.

285
00:14:59,417 --> 00:15:00,667
Is this where the party's at?

286
00:15:00,750 --> 00:15:02,083
- Migs?
- Mando!

287
00:15:02,167 --> 00:15:04,583
- Happy birthday!
- It's not my birthday.

288
00:15:04,667 --> 00:15:06,458
Oh, that's good.
I didn't get you anything.

289
00:15:06,542 --> 00:15:10,375
Do you like my ride? I stole it
from a pirate junkyard on Jakku.

290
00:15:10,458 --> 00:15:13,208
Wait. Why would you do anything nice
for Mando?

291
00:15:13,292 --> 00:15:14,417
He put you in prison.

292
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:15,833
He's my buddy now.

293
00:15:15,917 --> 00:15:19,208
He busted me out to help him rescue
the kid after the Imperials kidnapped him.

294
00:15:19,292 --> 00:15:20,750
[stutters] Kidnapped?

295
00:15:20,833 --> 00:15:22,917
Oh! It's a wicked great story.

296
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,958
And I was there for at least 20% of it.

297
00:15:25,042 --> 00:15:27,208
So Mando wasn't alone anymore.

298
00:15:27,292 --> 00:15:29,583
He had a kid, but now he had to bring him

299
00:15:29,667 --> 00:15:31,125
to be with his own kind,

300
00:15:31,208 --> 00:15:35,292
the powerful guardians of justice
in the galaxy, the Jethros.

301
00:15:35,375 --> 00:15:37,333
- [all] Jedi!
- Right.

302
00:15:37,417 --> 00:15:39,625
- Jedis.
- Jedi!

303
00:15:39,708 --> 00:15:42,250
Okay, Jedi, get over yourself.

304
00:15:42,333 --> 00:15:44,000
Yourselves!

305
00:15:44,083 --> 00:15:45,375
All right?

306
00:15:45,458 --> 00:15:48,542
So, anyway, Mando heard
there was another Mandalorian

307
00:15:48,625 --> 00:15:51,417
<i>and Mos Pelgo,
who could help him find some Jedi.</i>

308
00:15:51,500 --> 00:15:55,417
<i>But when he got there, it wasn't
a Mandalorian, it was just a regular guy.</i>

309
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:57,583
<i>A rugged marshal named Cobb Salad.</i>

310
00:15:57,667 --> 00:16:01,000
Vanth. The name is Cobb Vanth.

311
00:16:01,083 --> 00:16:02,625
<i>Okay, fine!</i>

312
00:16:02,708 --> 00:16:04,750
- Cobb Vanth.
- Thank you.

313
00:16:04,833 --> 00:16:07,458
He was wearing some other guy's armor.

314
00:16:07,542 --> 00:16:09,500
Oh! You'll never guess whose armor it was.

315
00:16:09,583 --> 00:16:11,500
It's a big name. Very famous.

316
00:16:11,583 --> 00:16:13,375
So spoil it!

317
00:16:13,458 --> 00:16:17,000
Mando believed the armor
should only be worn by a Mandalorian.

318
00:16:17,083 --> 00:16:19,208
So the marshal proposed a deal.

319
00:16:19,292 --> 00:16:21,167
I'll tell you what. You can have the armor

320
00:16:21,250 --> 00:16:24,542
if you help me and my people
here with a problem.

321
00:16:24,625 --> 00:16:26,833
[sighs in exasperation] Let me guess.

322
00:16:26,917 --> 00:16:28,917
I have to fight a monster.

323
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,292
No, you don't have to fight a monster.

324
00:16:31,375 --> 00:16:33,250
You have to fight a dragon.

325
00:16:34,625 --> 00:16:36,750
[roaring]

326
00:16:36,833 --> 00:16:38,708
- [whimpers]
- Here we go again.

327
00:16:38,792 --> 00:16:41,542
I need you to loan me
a bantha strapped with explosives.

328
00:16:41,625 --> 00:16:45,125
Well, you're in luck, because I always
keep a couple of those lying around.

329
00:16:45,208 --> 00:16:46,917
[grunts]

330
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:48,667
[roaring]

331
00:16:48,750 --> 00:16:51,833
- [bell dinging]
- Dragon, come to dinner!

332
00:16:59,292 --> 00:17:01,750
[Mando] This is going to stink.

333
00:17:01,833 --> 00:17:04,042
- [roaring]
- [gasps]

334
00:17:06,333 --> 00:17:07,708
[belches]

335
00:17:07,792 --> 00:17:09,083
[beeps]

336
00:17:13,750 --> 00:17:15,417
[Migs] Mando saved the day.

337
00:17:15,500 --> 00:17:19,083
<i>And if he blew up two more monsters,
he'd get a free sandwich.</i>

338
00:17:19,167 --> 00:17:23,417
{\an8}Try the roast womp rat on rye.
It's to die for.

339
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:24,958
[Migs] <i>Mando left with the armor</i>

340
00:17:25,042 --> 00:17:28,167
<i>and a lead on where to find some Jedi
to help the kid.</i>

341
00:17:28,250 --> 00:17:32,125
And you won't believe
all the crazy stuff that happened next.

342
00:17:32,208 --> 00:17:35,458
This is the 80% part that I wasn't
there for, but here we go anyway.

343
00:17:35,542 --> 00:17:38,417
<i>First, he had to take this frog lady
to meet a frog husband.</i>

344
00:17:38,500 --> 00:17:39,875
<i>But they had a crash landing.</i>

345
00:17:39,958 --> 00:17:43,042
<i>And Mando had to fight off
another giant monster.</i>

346
00:17:43,125 --> 00:17:45,083
<i>This time, a big spider.</i>

347
00:17:45,167 --> 00:17:49,417
<i>The frog husband sent Mando
to meet this lady Mando named Bo-Katan.</i>

348
00:17:49,500 --> 00:17:52,583
<i>They got in a crazy battle,
and then Bo-Katan told them...</i>

349
00:17:52,667 --> 00:17:55,667
I gotta get that dark saber thing
from Moff Bad Guy

350
00:17:55,750 --> 00:17:57,875
and reclaim the throne of Mandalore.

351
00:17:57,958 --> 00:18:00,125
Good luck with that, but I'm outie.

352
00:18:00,208 --> 00:18:04,083
[Migs] <i>So Mando and the kid went back
to Nevarro and fought off pirates.</i>

353
00:18:04,167 --> 00:18:05,250
[grunts]

354
00:18:06,625 --> 00:18:09,792
[Migs] <i>Then they found
the great Jedi, Ahsoka Tano.</i>

355
00:18:09,875 --> 00:18:11,000
<i>And she was all like...</i>

356
00:18:11,083 --> 00:18:12,583
Pretty snazzy entrance, huh?

357
00:18:12,667 --> 00:18:15,583
Ever see anybody spin
two of these light up dealies?

358
00:18:15,667 --> 00:18:18,708
[Migs] <i>Mando and Ahsoka teamed up
to defeat an evil tyrant</i>

359
00:18:18,792 --> 00:18:20,500
<i>and free a whole town.</i>

360
00:18:20,583 --> 00:18:24,208
<i>Ahsoka sent Mando to a planet where
the kid could reach out to the other Jedi.</i>

361
00:18:24,292 --> 00:18:25,917
<i>But what they didn't know was</i>

362
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,208
<i>Moff Bad Guy put a tracking beacon
on Mando's ship.</i>

363
00:18:28,292 --> 00:18:29,292
- [chuckles]
- [alarm blaring]

364
00:18:29,375 --> 00:18:31,833
<i>So Moff Bad Guy
was on his way to take the kid</i>

365
00:18:31,917 --> 00:18:34,250
<i>who Mando finally found out
his name!</i>

366
00:18:34,333 --> 00:18:37,208
He is called Goo-Goo.

367
00:18:37,292 --> 00:18:40,042
Grogu. His name is Grogu.

368
00:18:40,125 --> 00:18:41,667
At least I didn't call him Baby Yoda!

369
00:18:42,500 --> 00:18:46,417
So Mando got the kid to the Jedi place
where he could connect to the Jedi

370
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:49,333
<i>using that Jedi mind thing
that all the Jedi do.</i>

371
00:18:49,417 --> 00:18:51,333
Are you happy now that I got it right?

372
00:18:53,625 --> 00:18:56,208
- [Mando] Is that a Jedi?
- [Migs] <i>It wasn't a Jedi.</i>

373
00:18:56,292 --> 00:18:57,917
<i>It was a mystery adversary.</i>

374
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:04,000
<i>Another bounty hunter, the very same one
whose armor Cob Vanth gave to Mando,</i>

375
00:19:04,083 --> 00:19:07,208
<i>probably the most famous
bounty hunter of all!</i>

376
00:19:07,292 --> 00:19:10,583
- [whooping]
- Go ahead. You tell it. It

377
00:19:10,667 --> 00:19:14,292
It was Boba Fett
and he was with Fennec Shand.

378
00:19:16,500 --> 00:19:18,000
[Mando] Hey, that's my armor!

379
00:19:18,083 --> 00:19:20,167
I fought off a big monster to get it.

380
00:19:20,250 --> 00:19:22,833
I lost it in the stomach
of a bigger monster!

381
00:19:22,917 --> 00:19:23,958
[Peli] Uh, guys.

382
00:19:24,042 --> 00:19:26,500
guys, I have a better ship.

383
00:19:26,583 --> 00:19:28,208
My ship is way better.

384
00:19:28,292 --> 00:19:30,875
You can't even tell which part
is the front and which is the back.

385
00:19:30,958 --> 00:19:32,458
That's what's so great about it.

386
00:19:32,542 --> 00:19:37,833
Hey! Why don't you two stop
your ship measuring contest and look up!

387
00:19:41,167 --> 00:19:42,417
They blew up my ship.

388
00:19:42,500 --> 00:19:43,708
He left mine alone.

389
00:19:43,792 --> 00:19:45,083
They know how great it is.

390
00:19:45,167 --> 00:19:47,083
Enough about the ships!

391
00:19:47,167 --> 00:19:48,292
The kid is in trouble.

392
00:19:48,375 --> 00:19:50,250
[dramatic music playing]

393
00:19:52,208 --> 00:19:53,292
Yoink!

394
00:19:54,833 --> 00:19:56,167
Grogu!

395
00:20:00,292 --> 00:20:01,375
[whistles]

396
00:20:02,917 --> 00:20:05,667
How do you like me now, Mando?

397
00:20:05,750 --> 00:20:09,583
I didn't like you before,
and now I like you even less.

398
00:20:09,667 --> 00:20:11,833
That makes sense!

399
00:20:11,917 --> 00:20:13,167
Bye.

400
00:20:14,292 --> 00:20:15,542
[Migs] <i>Mando was devastated.</i>

401
00:20:15,625 --> 00:20:18,375
He knew he had to save Grogu
from those evil imps.

402
00:20:18,458 --> 00:20:20,708
But now he had a group
of friends to help him.

403
00:20:20,792 --> 00:20:22,958
And that's pretty good where I come from.

404
00:20:23,042 --> 00:20:25,167
Huh. Where do you come from?

405
00:20:25,250 --> 00:20:27,083
Where else? South Bespin!

406
00:20:33,917 --> 00:20:37,708
Your special blood
is going to make me invincible.

407
00:20:37,792 --> 00:20:40,208
Those are my reasons.

408
00:20:40,292 --> 00:20:41,500
[whimpers]

409
00:20:41,583 --> 00:20:43,958
Yes. Accept your fate.

410
00:20:44,042 --> 00:20:45,292
It is your destiny.

411
00:20:45,375 --> 00:20:48,333
- [whimpering]
- You don't have to overdo it.

412
00:20:48,417 --> 00:20:49,500
[grunting]

413
00:20:49,583 --> 00:20:50,750
Why are you--

414
00:20:53,750 --> 00:20:55,833
[beeping]

415
00:20:55,917 --> 00:20:57,292
[screams, grunts]

416
00:20:57,875 --> 00:20:58,875
[groans]

417
00:20:58,958 --> 00:21:00,125
[Migs] <i>It was on.</i>

418
00:21:00,208 --> 00:21:04,125
<i>Mando battled his way onto the ship
with the help of Bo-Katan.</i>

419
00:21:04,208 --> 00:21:06,083
- It was awesome.
- [both grunting]

420
00:21:06,167 --> 00:21:07,625
I got you now.

421
00:21:07,708 --> 00:21:09,125
- [laughs wickedly]
- [grunts]

422
00:21:09,208 --> 00:21:11,083
[yells]

423
00:21:17,167 --> 00:21:18,250
[Mando] Come on.

424
00:21:18,417 --> 00:21:20,417
- [guns cocking]
- [elevator dings]

425
00:21:24,583 --> 00:21:26,458
- [swishing]
- [gunfire]

426
00:21:29,250 --> 00:21:30,750
[R2-D2 beeping]

427
00:21:34,625 --> 00:21:38,917
[Migs] <i>The battle ended with the arrival
of the most famous Jedi of them all.</i>

428
00:21:41,292 --> 00:21:44,417
It looks like you were expecting us
to know who you are.

429
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:46,792
I'm Luke Skywalker.

430
00:21:48,625 --> 00:21:50,917
My father was Darth Vader?

431
00:21:52,500 --> 00:21:55,083
Oh, come on! I'm kind of a big deal!

432
00:21:55,167 --> 00:21:57,958
[Mando] Mm. If you say so.

433
00:21:58,042 --> 00:22:01,375
[sighs] I was beckoned by the call
of a young one named Grogu.

434
00:22:01,458 --> 00:22:03,458
- Where is he?
- At your feet.

435
00:22:03,542 --> 00:22:04,750
[speaking indistinctly]

436
00:22:04,833 --> 00:22:06,083
You're not very big.

437
00:22:06,167 --> 00:22:07,708
- [groans]
- Ugh!

438
00:22:07,792 --> 00:22:10,083
Right, right. Size matters not.

439
00:22:10,167 --> 00:22:13,042
He needs to be trained. By a Jedi.

440
00:22:13,125 --> 00:22:16,917
I know.
Can I have a moment with him?

441
00:22:18,792 --> 00:22:20,000
Kid.

442
00:22:20,083 --> 00:22:22,500
I guess this is goodbye.

443
00:22:22,583 --> 00:22:26,000
I have to let you see
my face this one time.

444
00:22:31,833 --> 00:22:33,250
Goodbye, Grogu.

445
00:22:33,333 --> 00:22:39,417
I hope I see you again,
maybe in a whole other series of events.

446
00:22:49,708 --> 00:22:51,917
[Migs] <i>And so the kid left with that
Luke guy</i>

447
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:54,333
<i>and his little beepee-boopy friend.</i>

448
00:22:54,417 --> 00:22:58,250
Grogu had finally found his family,
but Mando had lost his.

449
00:22:58,333 --> 00:23:00,583
[all sobbing]

450
00:23:01,583 --> 00:23:03,417
Don't worry, it all worked out.

451
00:23:03,500 --> 00:23:04,833
He's here, isn't he?

452
00:23:04,917 --> 00:23:07,958
[all cheering]

453
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:13,833
We tracked that thieving Migs
and the ship he stole from us

454
00:23:13,917 --> 00:23:16,750
to the Mos Eisley Cantina
on Tatooine.

455
00:23:16,833 --> 00:23:21,375
But get this, he's at a party
with The Mandalorian

456
00:23:21,458 --> 00:23:23,958
<i>and that little green kid!</i>

457
00:23:24,042 --> 00:23:25,667
Our archenemies!

458
00:23:25,750 --> 00:23:27,500
Well, The Mandalorian

459
00:23:27,583 --> 00:23:32,625
may have wiped us out of Nevarro,
but today, we pirates will triumph!

460
00:23:32,708 --> 00:23:34,208
[all cheering]

461
00:23:34,292 --> 00:23:37,167
<i>You go out and collect
every pirate in the sector,</i>

462
00:23:37,250 --> 00:23:41,625
<i>and when you have them all together,
launch an attack on that cantina!</i>

463
00:23:41,708 --> 00:23:43,708
[laughs wickedly]

464
00:23:43,792 --> 00:23:47,792
<i>We shall leave our enemies reeling!</i>

465
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:52,375
- [upbeat music playing]
- [indistinct chatter]

466
00:23:52,458 --> 00:23:53,542
[squealing]

467
00:23:54,583 --> 00:23:56,500
[whimpering]

468
00:23:56,583 --> 00:23:58,875
Hey, take it easy
with the little guy.

469
00:23:58,958 --> 00:24:00,083
Okay, that's it.

470
00:24:00,167 --> 00:24:02,375
This party is a bit too off the hook.

471
00:24:02,458 --> 00:24:05,875
- Ah, yeah!
- The kid and I should be heading home.

472
00:24:05,958 --> 00:24:08,833
- [all groaning]
- You can't leave now.

473
00:24:08,917 --> 00:24:10,667
All the guests haven't arrived.

474
00:24:10,750 --> 00:24:13,167
You have so many friends who want
to see you.

475
00:24:13,250 --> 00:24:14,792
That sounds exhausting.

476
00:24:14,875 --> 00:24:16,958
You're gonna make me cry
and you know I don't cry.

477
00:24:17,042 --> 00:24:18,500
- [Grogu whines]
- [groans]

478
00:24:18,583 --> 00:24:21,167
You see this sad face? It can get sadder.

479
00:24:21,250 --> 00:24:22,708
We really have to go.

480
00:24:23,333 --> 00:24:24,792
[somber instrumental music playing]

481
00:24:24,875 --> 00:24:27,167
Okay, fine! We'll stay.

482
00:24:27,250 --> 00:24:28,583
[all cheering]

483
00:24:28,667 --> 00:24:30,417
The story continues.

484
00:24:30,500 --> 00:24:33,417
Oh! Oh! Mando, tell us what happened
after Grogu left with Luke Skywalker.

485
00:24:33,500 --> 00:24:37,167
And what did Boba Fett do
after he fought the Imperials with you?

486
00:24:37,250 --> 00:24:40,208
That's his story,
and he's not here to tell it.

487
00:24:40,292 --> 00:24:44,833
Even if he was, Boba Fett is not one
to trumpet his own accomplishments.

488
00:24:44,917 --> 00:24:46,250
[trumpets playing]

489
00:24:46,333 --> 00:24:49,083
Felicitations upon this festive gathering!

490
00:24:49,167 --> 00:24:53,458
presenting the most excellent
Daimyo of Tatooine,

491
00:24:53,542 --> 00:24:55,708
the sort of son of Jango Fett.

492
00:24:55,792 --> 00:24:57,833
Boba Fett!

493
00:24:57,917 --> 00:25:01,208
And his guests Fennec Shand
and Krrsantan!

494
00:25:01,292 --> 00:25:03,458
[trumpets]

495
00:25:03,542 --> 00:25:05,750
Just ignore me. I'm not here.

496
00:25:05,833 --> 00:25:08,167
A little over the top, don't you think?

497
00:25:08,250 --> 00:25:11,458
When you spend months
eating dirt in the desert

498
00:25:11,542 --> 00:25:15,042
you can tell me how to live
when things start to go good.

499
00:25:15,125 --> 00:25:18,833
[gasps] You're Boba Fett,
the greatest bounty hunter of them all.

500
00:25:18,917 --> 00:25:20,417
He's okay.

501
00:25:20,500 --> 00:25:24,250
[stutters] Tell us how you got to be
Daimyo on Tatooine.

502
00:25:24,333 --> 00:25:27,250
No, no. I want to know how Mando
got Grogu back.

503
00:25:27,333 --> 00:25:29,500
Well, I want to hear about Boba Fett.

504
00:25:29,583 --> 00:25:30,708
Good sirs!

505
00:25:30,792 --> 00:25:35,458
The two stories you wish to hear
are serendipitously intertwined,

506
00:25:35,542 --> 00:25:40,000
and both end with the victory
of the heroic Boba Fett.

507
00:25:40,083 --> 00:25:43,833
Gather round and I shall delight you
with this glorious tale.

508
00:25:43,917 --> 00:25:46,500
It's a whole actual book?

509
00:25:46,583 --> 00:25:47,917
Not a big reader, huh?

510
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:51,833
I have to get up early in the morning,
skip a few chapters.

511
00:25:51,917 --> 00:25:54,208
- I live to serve.
- [Grogu coos]

512
00:25:54,292 --> 00:25:57,292
Boba Fett and Fennec Shand
returned to Tatooine,

513
00:25:57,375 --> 00:26:01,250
<i>where Boba Fett took care
of some unfinished business</i>

514
00:26:01,333 --> 00:26:04,750
<i>at the domicile of his former employer.</i>

515
00:26:06,750 --> 00:26:08,542
[speaking Huttese] <i>Die wonna wonga.</i>

516
00:26:08,625 --> 00:26:09,667
[guns cocking]

517
00:26:09,750 --> 00:26:12,000
<i>No wanna wonga!</i>

518
00:26:13,458 --> 00:26:17,000
[majordomo in English] <i>While Boba Fett
settled into his new Daimyo-citude,</i>

519
00:26:17,083 --> 00:26:19,542
<i>The Mandalorian
was on a quest of his own.</i>

520
00:26:19,625 --> 00:26:22,375
<i>Sadly, the razor crest was no more.</i>

521
00:26:22,458 --> 00:26:25,417
<i>So he visited Peli Motto
to acquire a new vehicle.</i>

522
00:26:25,500 --> 00:26:29,250
I want to go see the kid,
just to make sure he's safe.

523
00:26:29,333 --> 00:26:30,375
Oh, you're so cute.

524
00:26:30,458 --> 00:26:34,417
Admit it. You love the little guy
and you miss him. We won't tease you.

525
00:26:34,500 --> 00:26:37,625
Fine! Yes, I... I miss him.

526
00:26:37,708 --> 00:26:40,083
[all giggling]

527
00:26:41,208 --> 00:26:44,625
When I see Grogu,
I'm going to give him this.

528
00:26:44,708 --> 00:26:46,500
Very, very funny. That's funny.

529
00:26:46,583 --> 00:26:47,625
What's the real gift?

530
00:26:47,708 --> 00:26:51,417
That's it. It's a suit of chain mail
made from Beskar steel.

531
00:26:51,500 --> 00:26:53,917
Right. Right, right.
You know, kids hate clothes.

532
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:58,458
They want a nice speeder bike or something
with tassels on the handlebars.

533
00:26:58,542 --> 00:27:00,667
Something like that.
You know, something that moves.

534
00:27:00,750 --> 00:27:03,375
Beskar is sacred to all Mandalorians!

535
00:27:03,458 --> 00:27:05,375
Ugh, fine! You do you.

536
00:27:05,458 --> 00:27:06,667
I'll help you go see the kid.

537
00:27:06,750 --> 00:27:08,125
I got a new ship for you.

538
00:27:08,208 --> 00:27:12,375
I hope you're wearing socks
because they're about to get knocked off!

539
00:27:12,458 --> 00:27:14,667
Ta-da! Isn't it great?

540
00:27:14,750 --> 00:27:15,917
Uh...

541
00:27:16,000 --> 00:27:18,875
Only used once
by a 10-year-old on Boonta Eve.

542
00:27:18,958 --> 00:27:20,750
Nice kid. Really hated sand.

543
00:27:21,417 --> 00:27:22,417
No.

544
00:27:22,500 --> 00:27:24,042
Right, right, right, right, right.
Not for you, not for you.

545
00:27:24,125 --> 00:27:26,500
I got it, I got it, I got it, I got it.
How about this?

546
00:27:26,583 --> 00:27:27,667
Hard pass.

547
00:27:27,750 --> 00:27:30,292
Picky, picky, picky.
There's plenty more to choose from.

548
00:27:30,375 --> 00:27:31,833
Nope. Uh-huh.

549
00:27:31,917 --> 00:27:33,542
Wow. No!

550
00:27:33,667 --> 00:27:36,500
- [beeping]
- [Mando] No way! Never.

551
00:27:36,583 --> 00:27:38,708
You are a tough customer.

552
00:27:38,792 --> 00:27:42,292
All right. I was saving this
last one for you. Russell!

553
00:27:42,375 --> 00:27:43,583
Hit it.

554
00:27:44,250 --> 00:27:46,958
It's a Naboo N-1 Starfighter.

555
00:27:47,042 --> 00:27:49,958
This beauty was used
by the Royal Security Force

556
00:27:50,042 --> 00:27:54,042
during the Clone Wars,
and it's got the battle scars to prove it.

557
00:27:54,125 --> 00:27:56,667
And because you hate droids
and I like you,

558
00:27:56,750 --> 00:28:00,167
I've replaced the Astromech slot
with a seat for that

559
00:28:00,250 --> 00:28:02,375
special little green-eared
someone in your life.

560
00:28:02,458 --> 00:28:05,167
Total retail price?
You couldn't afford it.

561
00:28:05,250 --> 00:28:09,083
My asking price?
Give that kid a big hug for me.

562
00:28:09,167 --> 00:28:10,292
Sold.

563
00:28:10,375 --> 00:28:12,167
- [keys jingling]
- [whistles]

564
00:28:13,667 --> 00:28:19,125
So The Mandalorian flew off to pay
a visit to his diminutive green ward.

565
00:28:19,208 --> 00:28:23,875
This proved to be a case
of easier said than done.

566
00:28:23,958 --> 00:28:25,583
Grogu, it's me!

567
00:28:25,667 --> 00:28:27,292
- Daddy!
- No!

568
00:28:27,375 --> 00:28:28,917
You cannot see him.

569
00:28:29,000 --> 00:28:30,833
He is my responsibility.

570
00:28:30,917 --> 00:28:32,375
- [grunts]
- [electricity crackling]

571
00:28:32,458 --> 00:28:33,458
[beeping]

572
00:28:33,542 --> 00:28:36,083
Okay! Take it easy, big guy.

573
00:28:36,167 --> 00:28:37,167
[beeping]

574
00:28:39,167 --> 00:28:43,833
I know you miss Grogu, and I sympathize,
but he is with Master Luke.

575
00:28:43,917 --> 00:28:47,292
We can't let Grogu's attachment
to you disrupt his training.

576
00:28:47,375 --> 00:28:49,333
Use the Force, Grogu.

577
00:28:49,417 --> 00:28:51,250
Pick up a rock.

578
00:28:53,458 --> 00:28:55,875
- Good.
- Ah! [chuckles]

579
00:28:59,667 --> 00:29:00,833
Very good!

580
00:29:02,083 --> 00:29:03,708
Stupid good.

581
00:29:03,792 --> 00:29:06,667
Wow. You're force building
at a high school level.

582
00:29:06,750 --> 00:29:09,083
[laughs] Ooh!

583
00:29:10,375 --> 00:29:12,625
- [coos]
- [grunts]

584
00:29:13,708 --> 00:29:16,292
We'll try again after lunch. [grunts]

585
00:29:16,375 --> 00:29:18,500
I don't want the kid to flunk.

586
00:29:18,583 --> 00:29:22,292
Eventually, Grogu
will have to choose his own path.

587
00:29:23,292 --> 00:29:25,667
- But for now...
- I'll go.

588
00:29:25,750 --> 00:29:27,750
But can you give him this?

589
00:29:28,125 --> 00:29:30,583
- [beeping]
- Yes, that's it.

590
00:29:30,667 --> 00:29:32,417
- That's the gift.
- [beeping]

591
00:29:32,500 --> 00:29:34,292
No, it's not a speeder bike.

592
00:29:34,375 --> 00:29:36,708
- It's precious Beskar steel!
- [grunts]

593
00:29:36,792 --> 00:29:39,083
No, he can't sell the steel
to buy a speeder bike.

594
00:29:39,167 --> 00:29:43,125
<i>So The Mandalorian returned
to Tatooine to assist Boba Fett,</i>

595
00:29:43,208 --> 00:29:46,583
<i>who is encountering fierce resistance
to his rule</i>

596
00:29:46,667 --> 00:29:49,958
<i>from the dreaded Pyke crime syndicate.</i>

597
00:29:50,042 --> 00:29:54,958
<i>The Mandalorian was a warrior,
and now he was back in his element.</i>

598
00:29:55,042 --> 00:29:58,167
I, regrettably, was not in my element.

599
00:29:58,250 --> 00:30:04,250
<i>While Mando, Fennec and their allies
waged a valiant fight, Boba Fett...</i>

600
00:30:04,333 --> 00:30:05,708
<i>ran away.</i>

601
00:30:05,792 --> 00:30:07,917
I went to get help! Tell it right!

602
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:09,833
Yes, great and merciful one.

603
00:30:09,917 --> 00:30:13,667
Boba Fett heroically ran away to get help.

604
00:30:13,750 --> 00:30:16,708
<i>Meanwhile, Luke Skywalker presented Grogu</i>

605
00:30:16,792 --> 00:30:19,667
<i>with the gift
The Mandalorian left behind.</i>

606
00:30:19,750 --> 00:30:20,792
[speaking indistinctly]

607
00:30:20,875 --> 00:30:24,833
The Force is strong with Grogu
but he cannot be distracted like this.

608
00:30:24,917 --> 00:30:27,333
He has to choose between his training
with me

609
00:30:27,417 --> 00:30:29,417
and reuniting with The Mandalorian.

610
00:30:29,500 --> 00:30:33,167
I think he's already made his choice.

611
00:30:33,250 --> 00:30:35,917
[laughing]

612
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:38,000
Yes. Yes, it's very you.

613
00:30:38,083 --> 00:30:39,292
Oh! [giggles]

614
00:30:39,375 --> 00:30:43,583
[sighs] I sure hope my next student
won't be this difficult.

615
00:30:43,667 --> 00:30:45,583
[dramatic music playing]

616
00:30:45,667 --> 00:30:47,208
[grunts]

617
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:51,958
<i>Things were looking bad
for The Mandalorian</i>

618
00:30:52,042 --> 00:30:56,833
<i>but then Boba Fett made
his triumphant, heroic return,</i>

619
00:30:56,917 --> 00:30:59,208
because he didn't really run away.

620
00:30:59,292 --> 00:31:01,500
He was always there.

621
00:31:01,583 --> 00:31:03,250
Now you're overdoing it.

622
00:31:03,333 --> 00:31:06,458
[dramatic music playing]

623
00:31:08,000 --> 00:31:10,750
Finally! A monster I can like!

624
00:31:10,833 --> 00:31:14,042
[yelps] I take that back!

625
00:31:14,125 --> 00:31:16,583
[grunting]

626
00:31:17,833 --> 00:31:20,125
Mando, stop playing with that rancor!

627
00:31:20,208 --> 00:31:22,333
[straining] It's playing with me!

628
00:31:22,417 --> 00:31:24,458
Good thing I brought somebody with me.

629
00:31:24,542 --> 00:31:25,542
[giggles]

630
00:31:25,625 --> 00:31:27,458
Kid! [grunting]

631
00:31:27,542 --> 00:31:30,875
- Am I happy... to see... you.
- [thudding]

632
00:31:30,958 --> 00:31:32,417
Use the Force!

633
00:31:32,500 --> 00:31:34,917
Knock this monster into the next galaxy.

634
00:31:36,792 --> 00:31:39,042
[growling]

635
00:31:41,417 --> 00:31:43,708
- [Grogu grunts]
- [Mando sighs]

636
00:31:43,792 --> 00:31:45,583
Putting it to sleep works, too.

637
00:31:45,667 --> 00:31:48,833
And so, with the help of the returning
Din Djarin,

638
00:31:48,917 --> 00:31:51,667
the great Daimyo Boba Fett

639
00:31:51,750 --> 00:31:55,542
defeated the Pykes
and brought peace to Mos Espa.

640
00:31:55,625 --> 00:32:00,958
For all of our firepower, in the end,
it was the little one who saved us.

641
00:32:01,042 --> 00:32:02,500
What? What about me?

642
00:32:02,583 --> 00:32:05,625
I brought him there from the spaceport.
I was his ride!

643
00:32:05,708 --> 00:32:07,542
Yes, congratulations.

644
00:32:07,625 --> 00:32:12,542
Things looked good for Mando and Grogu
but there was danger ahead.

645
00:32:12,625 --> 00:32:14,542
For unbeknownst to them,

646
00:32:14,625 --> 00:32:17,917
Moff Gideon had escaped
New Republic custody

647
00:32:18,000 --> 00:32:19,792
- and was closing--
- [all exclaiming]

648
00:32:19,875 --> 00:32:21,792
- [thudding]
- [all screaming]

649
00:32:21,875 --> 00:32:23,583
[yelling]

650
00:32:23,667 --> 00:32:26,833
- Hello, Mando.
- [guns cocking]

651
00:32:26,917 --> 00:32:29,917
Happy birthday to us.

652
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:33,000
It's not my birthday,
it's just a party!

653
00:32:33,083 --> 00:32:34,417
[Mando] Pirates.

654
00:32:34,500 --> 00:32:36,708
We won't be able
to hold them off on our own.

655
00:32:36,792 --> 00:32:42,292
I shall engage them diplomatically
and negotiate an amicable settlement.

656
00:32:42,792 --> 00:32:44,417
[lasers firing]

657
00:32:44,500 --> 00:32:47,875
Not so amicable. [whimpers]

658
00:32:47,958 --> 00:32:49,208
Nobody panic.

659
00:32:49,292 --> 00:32:52,292
Bo-Katan and her fellow Mandalorians
will be here soon,

660
00:32:52,375 --> 00:32:54,333
and they will help us. I know it.

661
00:32:54,417 --> 00:32:56,500
How can you be so sure?

662
00:32:56,583 --> 00:32:58,667
Because we defeated Moff Gideon together.

663
00:32:58,750 --> 00:33:02,083
Because we are heirs to a legacy
of commitment and devotion

664
00:33:02,167 --> 00:33:05,250
going back to the ancient
ancestors of Mandalore.

665
00:33:05,333 --> 00:33:07,875
And also because she's
sitting right over there.

666
00:33:07,958 --> 00:33:09,250
[grunts]

667
00:33:09,625 --> 00:33:11,792
No way I'd ever miss your party.

668
00:33:11,875 --> 00:33:13,542
Thanks for the invite, Peli.

669
00:33:13,625 --> 00:33:14,625
- [thudding]
- [all exclaiming]

670
00:33:18,333 --> 00:33:22,000
No more inspirational speeches, Mando.

671
00:33:22,083 --> 00:33:23,333
Give up.

672
00:33:23,417 --> 00:33:25,708
You'll have to come through all of us.

673
00:33:25,792 --> 00:33:28,750
But these guys first.
Got to adjust the hair for the helmet.

674
00:33:31,042 --> 00:33:33,583
- [all grunting]
- [guns firing]

675
00:33:34,583 --> 00:33:35,833
No! No, no, no.

676
00:33:35,917 --> 00:33:38,417
[exclaiming]

677
00:33:38,500 --> 00:33:41,333
[all exclaiming]

678
00:33:42,500 --> 00:33:43,708
[screaming]

679
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:47,042
Gonna need some help here.

680
00:33:48,667 --> 00:33:50,833
[all cheering]

681
00:33:50,917 --> 00:33:54,208
Wow! Boba Fett, you're the best.

682
00:33:54,292 --> 00:33:56,125
Hey, what are we? Bantha Poodoo?

683
00:33:56,208 --> 00:33:57,833
Welcome to my world.

684
00:33:57,917 --> 00:33:58,958
We're not safe yet.

685
00:33:59,042 --> 00:34:02,208
Those pirates will be back
with plenty of reinforcements.

686
00:34:02,292 --> 00:34:03,875
We're going to be all right.

687
00:34:03,958 --> 00:34:07,000
Just like in our final victory
over Moff Gideon on Mandalore.

688
00:34:07,083 --> 00:34:08,375
What did you do there?

689
00:34:08,458 --> 00:34:11,375
It's a good story. I will tell you.

690
00:34:11,458 --> 00:34:14,125
Does everybody have to tell a story?

691
00:34:14,208 --> 00:34:17,458
Yes! It's very inspiring.

692
00:34:18,583 --> 00:34:20,458
[sighs wearily] I'm sure it is.

693
00:34:20,542 --> 00:34:22,042
Go right ahead.

694
00:34:23,417 --> 00:34:26,333
Din Djarin had finally
reunited with Grogu.

695
00:34:26,417 --> 00:34:30,542
Now he needed to redeem himself
and reclaim his status as a Mandalorian.

696
00:34:30,625 --> 00:34:34,292
<i>So he and Grogu journeyed to be
with the armorer and her covert.</i>

697
00:34:34,375 --> 00:34:38,792
Din Djarin, you have proven
your valor in many battles,

698
00:34:38,875 --> 00:34:41,667
saved the Mandalorians from great harm,

699
00:34:41,750 --> 00:34:45,583
- and defeated five separate monsters.
- [beeps]

700
00:34:46,083 --> 00:34:48,875
Here is your free sandwich.

701
00:34:49,875 --> 00:34:52,750
So does this mean you won't punish me

702
00:34:52,833 --> 00:34:55,417
for taking off my helmet
when I said goodbye to Grogu?

703
00:34:55,500 --> 00:34:58,667
You still must be cast out as an apostate!

704
00:34:58,750 --> 00:35:00,833
I knew you'd understand.

705
00:35:00,917 --> 00:35:03,083
But the lore says I can be redeemed

706
00:35:03,167 --> 00:35:05,458
if I bathe in the living waters
of Mandalore.

707
00:35:05,542 --> 00:35:08,167
That will never happen.

708
00:35:08,250 --> 00:35:10,500
- And?
- It did happen!

709
00:35:10,583 --> 00:35:15,083
Oh, I'm glad I'm wearing a helmet,
because my face is bright red under here.

710
00:35:15,167 --> 00:35:17,667
It's all right.
We're in this together now.

711
00:35:17,750 --> 00:35:22,000
Yes, all the Mandalorians
were now joined in a common cause.

712
00:35:22,083 --> 00:35:23,458
<i>And just in time.</i>

713
00:35:25,125 --> 00:35:28,500
<i>Now that I have escaped
from my New Republic captors,</i>

714
00:35:28,583 --> 00:35:32,917
I will destroy the Mandalorians
once and for all.

715
00:35:33,000 --> 00:35:37,792
In a battle suit
made of pure Beskar steel.

716
00:35:37,875 --> 00:35:38,917
Yes.

717
00:35:39,708 --> 00:35:42,208
All of the galaxy will fear me!

718
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:46,042
Wrong color!

719
00:35:46,125 --> 00:35:48,500
This is for my beach party armor!

720
00:35:48,583 --> 00:35:53,125
[Bo-Katan] <i>Aware of Moff Gideon's threat,
Mando and Grogu returned to Nevarro,</i>

721
00:35:53,208 --> 00:35:57,667
where Greef Karga had a surprise in store!

722
00:35:57,750 --> 00:35:59,625
With Moff Gideon on the loose,

723
00:35:59,708 --> 00:36:02,500
I worry about you and the kid,

724
00:36:02,583 --> 00:36:05,292
so I have a gift for Grogu.

725
00:36:07,917 --> 00:36:09,667
[all cheering]

726
00:36:11,333 --> 00:36:13,625
The Anzellans
made you a new protector

727
00:36:13,708 --> 00:36:15,833
who's actually your old protector.

728
00:36:18,167 --> 00:36:19,583
Behold!

729
00:36:21,333 --> 00:36:24,167
This is IG-12.

730
00:36:24,250 --> 00:36:25,292
How are you?

731
00:36:26,500 --> 00:36:29,583
He cannot speak
unless Grogu is at the controls.

732
00:36:29,667 --> 00:36:32,375
Wait! Grogu can operate him
from his chest?

733
00:36:32,458 --> 00:36:33,583
Yes, yes.

734
00:36:33,667 --> 00:36:36,833
Grogu, are you speaking through IG-12 now?

735
00:36:36,917 --> 00:36:38,083
Yes yes.

736
00:36:38,167 --> 00:36:39,250
Are you kidding me?

737
00:36:39,875 --> 00:36:41,458
No, no.

738
00:36:41,542 --> 00:36:43,667
This is gonna annoy me, right?

739
00:36:43,750 --> 00:36:45,500
Probably, probably

740
00:36:45,583 --> 00:36:48,125
With Grogu even more powerful now,

741
00:36:48,208 --> 00:36:52,333
and the tribes of Mandalore
forged into one united clan,

742
00:36:52,417 --> 00:36:57,000
our combined forces launched an attack
on Moff Gideon's base.

743
00:36:57,083 --> 00:37:00,083
<i>The Imperials will feel my tongs!</i>

744
00:37:00,167 --> 00:37:04,667
I'm going to give them
such a pinch! For Mandalore!

745
00:37:04,750 --> 00:37:07,458
Oh! The dark saber is pretty good, too.

746
00:37:07,792 --> 00:37:11,250
[all screaming]

747
00:37:12,292 --> 00:37:14,958
- [dramatic music playing]
- [both grunting]

748
00:37:23,750 --> 00:37:25,583
[all yelling]

749
00:37:28,292 --> 00:37:31,292
[Bo-Katan] <i>Just when it looked like
it was lights out for Mando,</i>

750
00:37:31,375 --> 00:37:32,750
<i>he was rescued</i>

751
00:37:32,833 --> 00:37:34,625
[squealing] by Grogu!

752
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:37,542
No, no, no.

753
00:37:40,125 --> 00:37:41,458
[IG-12] Uh-oh! Uh-oh! Uh--

754
00:37:43,208 --> 00:37:44,542
[grunts]

755
00:37:45,083 --> 00:37:46,792
[yells]

756
00:37:47,875 --> 00:37:49,167
[grunts]

757
00:37:53,792 --> 00:37:55,583
[Moff] Bo-Katan and Din Djarin!

758
00:37:57,000 --> 00:37:58,750
Your story ends now.

759
00:37:59,375 --> 00:38:02,125
Does it smell like yellow paint in here?

760
00:38:02,208 --> 00:38:03,625
No, it does not!

761
00:38:03,708 --> 00:38:07,042
[all grunting]

762
00:38:13,583 --> 00:38:16,375
[grunting continues]

763
00:38:20,958 --> 00:38:22,625
[Moff cackles]

764
00:38:22,708 --> 00:38:25,708
[grunting]

765
00:38:33,417 --> 00:38:34,542
[grunts]

766
00:38:34,625 --> 00:38:36,792
Nothing can stop me now!

767
00:38:38,125 --> 00:38:42,083
Except a giant flaming ship
crashing into the planet.

768
00:38:43,875 --> 00:38:46,250
Very well. I'll be destroyed,

769
00:38:46,333 --> 00:38:47,667
but I'll take you with me.

770
00:38:47,750 --> 00:38:49,792
Nothing can save you from...

771
00:38:51,750 --> 00:38:54,333
Oh, right, the Force.

772
00:39:02,583 --> 00:39:06,500
[Bo-Katan] At last, Mandalore was returned
to the Mandalorians.

773
00:39:06,583 --> 00:39:10,583
Din Djarin adopted Grogu and vowed
to train him.

774
00:39:10,667 --> 00:39:14,458
You are now Din Grogu!

775
00:39:15,167 --> 00:39:17,250
[roars]

776
00:39:18,292 --> 00:39:22,625
And peace was restored
for a tiny bit.

777
00:39:22,708 --> 00:39:24,000
Whoa, whoa. What does that mean?

778
00:39:24,083 --> 00:39:25,167
What happened next?

779
00:39:25,250 --> 00:39:26,667
I can tell that one,

780
00:39:27,458 --> 00:39:30,792
and it is quite a story.

781
00:39:39,875 --> 00:39:42,417
Drop your popcorn. The pirates are back!

782
00:39:43,292 --> 00:39:45,292
[wicked laughter]

783
00:39:45,375 --> 00:39:46,958
Avast, Mandalorian!

784
00:39:50,500 --> 00:39:53,458
Today you will see your end.

785
00:39:53,542 --> 00:39:54,833
Gorian Shard?

786
00:39:54,917 --> 00:39:56,375
I thought you were destroyed.

787
00:39:56,458 --> 00:39:59,792
I am his nephew, Dorian Shard!

788
00:39:59,875 --> 00:40:01,375
Totally different guy.

789
00:40:01,500 --> 00:40:04,083
So what, are you, like,
a big plant or something?

790
00:40:04,167 --> 00:40:06,042
[groans] I am not a plant!

791
00:40:06,125 --> 00:40:10,583
I am plant-like, and you will pay
for what you did to my uncle.

792
00:40:10,667 --> 00:40:12,083
Fire!

793
00:40:12,792 --> 00:40:14,083
[Peli] Aah!

794
00:40:14,167 --> 00:40:15,708
[laughing maniacally]

795
00:40:15,792 --> 00:40:17,625
- [both grunting]
- Fall back!

796
00:40:17,708 --> 00:40:19,000
Get back inside!

797
00:40:19,083 --> 00:40:21,875
- [panting]
- Aah! Poodoo!

798
00:40:21,958 --> 00:40:23,042
Okay, that's it.

799
00:40:23,125 --> 00:40:25,417
We're done.
We can't beat Fern Boy out there.

800
00:40:25,500 --> 00:40:27,000
Got any more of those
self-destruct thingies?

801
00:40:27,083 --> 00:40:28,167
No self-destructing.

802
00:40:28,250 --> 00:40:31,083
Well, what else are we gonna do?
We're all alone here!

803
00:40:31,167 --> 00:40:33,500
No, I was alone.

804
00:40:33,583 --> 00:40:34,917
But not anymore.

805
00:40:35,000 --> 00:40:38,000
Now I have Grogu, and I have all of you.

806
00:40:38,083 --> 00:40:41,458
We are strong because we are a family,

807
00:40:41,542 --> 00:40:44,625
and because Grogu can move stuff
by just waving at it.

808
00:40:44,708 --> 00:40:47,458
Peli, you still have
those junkers in your yard?

809
00:40:47,542 --> 00:40:49,625
Do tauntaun smell bad on the outside?

810
00:40:49,708 --> 00:40:51,083
I have no idea.

811
00:40:51,167 --> 00:40:54,833
Trust me, they do. Whoo-hoo! P-ew!

812
00:40:54,917 --> 00:40:56,708
IG-11, cover us.

813
00:40:56,792 --> 00:40:58,125
I will comply.

814
00:41:02,250 --> 00:41:06,083
Pirates, you will fail,
because I am an assassin droid,

815
00:41:06,167 --> 00:41:09,792
like the three or four other
versions of myself before me.

816
00:41:12,833 --> 00:41:14,417
[all yelling]

817
00:41:17,708 --> 00:41:19,833
He's a dancing machine.

818
00:41:22,000 --> 00:41:24,958
Here you go.
My empire of junk.

819
00:41:25,042 --> 00:41:26,417
It's beautiful.

820
00:41:26,500 --> 00:41:28,833
Kid, do your thing.

821
00:41:38,792 --> 00:41:40,125
I am out of ammunition.

822
00:41:40,208 --> 00:41:42,833
Friends, you may come out
and support me now.

823
00:41:44,875 --> 00:41:46,292
I believe I have been pranked.

824
00:41:46,375 --> 00:41:47,625
[Mando] No, you haven't.

825
00:41:52,792 --> 00:41:57,125
Dorian Shard, go now before we uproot you!

826
00:41:57,208 --> 00:41:58,292
[laughs] Yeah!

827
00:41:58,375 --> 00:42:03,000
- You better leave!
- Put the petal to the metal! [laughs]

828
00:42:03,083 --> 00:42:07,292
Oh, for the last time, I am not a plant!
I have feet!

829
00:42:07,375 --> 00:42:08,667
Attack!

830
00:42:13,958 --> 00:42:15,417
[screeches]

831
00:42:15,500 --> 00:42:18,000
[exclaiming]

832
00:42:18,083 --> 00:42:19,458
[grunts]

833
00:42:22,458 --> 00:42:25,167
[shudders]

834
00:42:25,250 --> 00:42:27,667
First mate,
we are outnumbered on the ground.

835
00:42:27,750 --> 00:42:31,125
Prepare the heavy cannon
for orbital bombardment.

836
00:42:31,208 --> 00:42:32,583
[roars]

837
00:42:32,667 --> 00:42:36,792
[creaking]

838
00:42:40,583 --> 00:42:42,167
Oh, whoa!

839
00:42:43,875 --> 00:42:45,917
[grunts]

840
00:42:47,500 --> 00:42:49,500
[yelps, grunts]

841
00:42:50,458 --> 00:42:52,417
[yells]

842
00:42:54,208 --> 00:42:56,458
Hey pal, have a mynock on me!

843
00:42:56,542 --> 00:42:57,708
- Whoo!
- [screaming]

844
00:42:58,625 --> 00:43:02,375
Why didn't I get those hatches greased
when I had the chance?

845
00:43:02,458 --> 00:43:04,625
I need firepower!

846
00:43:05,500 --> 00:43:08,625
[exclaims] A 50-year-old baby!

847
00:43:08,708 --> 00:43:10,042
[laughs wickedly]

848
00:43:10,125 --> 00:43:12,292
Hey, you got your speeder bike!

849
00:43:12,375 --> 00:43:13,417
[coos]

850
00:43:13,500 --> 00:43:16,792
Pirate flagship, open fire!

851
00:43:17,583 --> 00:43:19,042
- [squeals]
- Huh?

852
00:43:24,042 --> 00:43:25,375
My ship!

853
00:43:25,458 --> 00:43:27,375
All my stuff was on there.

854
00:43:29,125 --> 00:43:30,167
[groans]

855
00:43:30,250 --> 00:43:32,667
Got anything to say now, Dorian?

856
00:43:32,750 --> 00:43:35,917
Eh! You wouldn't hurt
an innocent houseplant, would you?

857
00:43:36,000 --> 00:43:38,083
See? [grunts]

858
00:43:38,708 --> 00:43:41,542
Hey, look, he's soiling himself!

859
00:43:41,625 --> 00:43:45,042
[exclaiming]

860
00:43:48,500 --> 00:43:50,375
Mando, you did it!

861
00:43:50,458 --> 00:43:55,708
No, we did it because I was able
to put down my armor, figuratively,

862
00:43:55,792 --> 00:43:58,292
and let all of you into my life.

863
00:43:58,375 --> 00:44:00,958
So... I guess I did do it.

864
00:44:01,042 --> 00:44:02,625
That's what I meant, you dum-dum.

865
00:44:02,708 --> 00:44:05,417
And though this wasn't
the assignment I was expecting,

866
00:44:05,500 --> 00:44:09,292
I'm glad you put on a fake mustache
and tricked us into coming here.

867
00:44:09,375 --> 00:44:11,583
Does that mean...

868
00:44:13,458 --> 00:44:18,250
Yes, I am ready to enjoy
the party with my friends.

869
00:44:18,333 --> 00:44:19,417
Hit it!

870
00:44:20,333 --> 00:44:22,292
[upbeat music playing]

871
00:44:23,167 --> 00:44:24,958
[camera shutter clicking]